slim-qcom-ngd-ctrl: driver_override moved from platform_device into struct device

Same change as upstream 6.18 qcom-ngd-ctrl.c: device_set_driver_override(&pdev->dev, name).
The NGD child device still binds only to the ngd driver. Needed for Bluetooth audio
(bt_fm_slim over the LPASS slimbus, loaded on 5.4 as slimbus_ngd + bt_fm_slim).

--- a/bsp612/soc-repo/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/bsp612/soc-repo/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1925,10 +1925,9 @@
 		ngd->id = id;
 		ngd->pdev->dev.parent = parent;
 
-		ret = driver_set_override(&ngd->pdev->dev,
-					  &ngd->pdev->driver_override,
-					  QCOM_SLIM_NGD_DRV_NAME,
-					  strlen(QCOM_SLIM_NGD_DRV_NAME));
+		/* 6.18: the override lives in struct device (as upstream) */
+		ret = device_set_driver_override(&ngd->pdev->dev,
+						 QCOM_SLIM_NGD_DRV_NAME);
 		if (ret) {
 			platform_device_put(ngd->pdev);
 			kfree(ngd);
